        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T17:59:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Experimentally, it seems like the default VBUS monitoring implementation detects vSinkDisconnect/vSafe0V at too high of a voltage. I think that just uses the PPC?\n\nSo it could be that the PPC vSafe0V threshold is a little off. Maybe less likely, it could be that we\u0027re using the TCPC threshold detection in EXTENDED_STATUS, and that\u0027s a little off compared to the TCPC ADC. Either way, I don\u0027t have a hypothesis about why that might be the case yet.",
      "parentUuid": "4887fc20_2679cd2e",
      "revId": "26a38ec3b26a2ed8a44a27b7d9415deba8f2321a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
